 {"id":"fabro-d5a6","title":"web: files tab refuses large diffs ('too large to render inline') — offer truncated/per-record rendering","status":"open","type":"bug","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-09-05T07:56:35.110Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-05T07:56:35.110Z","description":"User report 2026-09-05: in a run's Files tab, the diff for .seeds/issues.jsonl (182 records / ~264KB) is refused with '.seeds/issues.jsonl too large to render inline', so revisor-filed seeds cannot be reviewed in the UI at all. Wanted: at minimum a truncated diff with explicit cut + full-diff download; ideally per-record (JSONL line) diff rendering so one revisor cycle's additions are readable. Basis: revisor run on denkhaus, Files tab, 2026-09-05.","labels":["web","ux"]}
 {"id":"fabro-71b9","title":"web: kanban run tiles — show run date, workflow name, and workflow version","status":"open","type":"feature","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-09-05T08:41:02.820Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-05T08:41:02.820Z","description":"User request 2026-09-05: the kanban run tiles currently show only title, diff status, repo, and PR numbers. Wanted additionally on each tile: (1) the run date (created_at or last activity), (2) the workflow name, (3) the workflow version. The workflow_version_id is content-derived (SHA-256 of the canonical workflow package) and exposed by the API run record as workflow.workflow_version_id (runs list since ADR-0015 engine change, 2026-09-05); render a short form (first ~12 hex chars) so tiles stay compact. Complements fabro-d5a6 (large-diff rendering); together they close the run-identity visibility gap in the UI.","labels":["web","ux","workflows"]}
 {"id":"fabro-56c2","title":"State the fs_hide shell bypass plainly in develop prompts","status":"closed","type":"task","priority":1,"createdAt":"2026-09-05T09:56:55.646Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-05T10:13:37.676Z","description":"In .fabro/workflows/develop/prompts/implementer.md (Platform scope section) and prompts/planner.md (ADR-0015 stale-basis step), replace the claim 'writes are denied (fabro-1dae fs_hide)' — disproved in the target run — with explicit guidance that for platform-targeting seeds, .fabro/** reads/writes go through the shell because fs_hide binds tool calls only (implementer read_file denied at seq 145, then 3 discovery calls before a python3 heredoc edit at seq 174; planner forced into shell fallback at seq 83). Effect: 3-4 tool calls and 2-3 LLM turns saved per platform-targeting seed, and prompts stop asserting unenforced behavior. Basis: run 01M1RF53QWM4Q5REBVSG9F9Y43, workflow version absent, commit 3ca43b1cd19c8cf291668bdbdc4a1fbbc321e2ec","labels":["revision"],"closedAt":"2026-09-05T10:13:37.676Z"}
-{"id":"fabro-7e88","title":"Fast-path sd show <id> in planner when the goal names a seed id","status":"open","type":"task","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-09-05T09:57:01.637Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-05T09:57:01.637Z","description":"Add one rule to .fabro/workflows/develop/prompts/planner.md step 1: if the goal names a seed id, run 'sd show <id> --format json' first and only fall back to 'sd ready' if the id does not resolve. In the target run the goal contained fabro-37a6 yet step 1 ran 'sd ready --limit 200', pulling 118 issues / 13.9 KB truncated output next to the sd show in the same batch (seq 65-68). Effect: ~14 KB less context and one fewer call in the run's most expensive stage (planner = 63% of run cost). Basis: run 01M1RF53QWM4Q5REBVSG9F9Y43, workflow version absent, commit 3ca43b1cd19c8cf291668bdbdc4a1fbbc321e2ec","labels":["revision"]}
+{"id":"fabro-7e88","title":"Fast-path sd show <id> in planner when the goal names a seed id","status":"in_progress","type":"task","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-09-05T09:57:01.637Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-05T10:44:11.214Z","description":"Add one rule to .fabro/workflows/develop/prompts/planner.md step 1: if the goal names a seed id, run 'sd show <id> --format json' first and only fall back to 'sd ready' if the id does not resolve. In the target run the goal contained fabro-37a6 yet step 1 ran 'sd ready --limit 200', pulling 118 issues / 13.9 KB truncated output next to the sd show in the same batch (seq 65-68). Effect: ~14 KB less context and one fewer call in the run's most expensive stage (planner = 63% of run cost). Basis: run 01M1RF53QWM4Q5REBVSG9F9Y43, workflow version absent, commit 3ca43b1cd19c8cf291668bdbdc4a1fbbc321e2ec","labels":["revision"]}
 {"id":"fabro-3839","title":"Lint filed seeds for resolvable basis refs and tool-name typos","status":"open","type":"task","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-09-05T09:57:08.037Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-05T09:57:08.037Z","description":"In the seed-intake path of the revisor/improve workflow (the stage writing .seeds/issues.jsonl), require a resolvable run-id/Basis line per ADR-0015 and flag tool-name typos against the pinned-toolchain list. Seed fabro-37a6 shipped three defects the planner burned high-effort reasoning resolving: 'sd' as a typo for 'sed', unresolvable evidence ref fabro-28e8, and a call-site count (~24) conflicting with the recorded one (~40). Effect: planner passes stop paying the contradiction-resolution premium and ambiguous briefs — a known reviewer ping-pong driver — are caught before a run starts. Basis: run 01M1RF53QWM4Q5REBVSG9F9Y43, workflow version absent, commit 3ca43b1cd19c8cf291668bdbdc4a1fbbc321e2ec","labels":["revision"]}
 {"id":"fabro-a0e3","title":"Fix Pipeline progress header's unique-node denominator","status":"open","type":"task","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-09-05T09:57:15.814Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-05T09:57:15.814Z","description":"Fix the 'Pipeline progress: 0 of 6 stages completed' agent-stage preamble header (unique-node denominator in the preamble rendering) so already-completed stages count: in the target run the implementer header reported 0 of 6 with planner done, misinforming the agent about loop state. Effect: correct loop-state information in every stage preamble. Basis: run 01M1RF53QWM4Q5REBVSG9F9Y43, workflow version absent, commit 3ca43b1cd19c8cf291668bdbdc4a1fbbc321e2ec","labels":["revision"]}
 {"id":"fabro-270c","title":"Make the journal payload shape retry-proof in develop prompts","status":"open","type":"task","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-09-05T10:21:23.903Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-05T10:21:23.903Z","description":"In run 01M1RGQHJ5RV8Y28M2GH97XGEZ the planner's first final answer emitted malformed journal JSON ([\"observations\" : \"none\"]); the routing validator rejected it ('key must be a string at line 1 column 2647', seq 91) and the retry burned ~13 s plus a full-context re-read (~$0.01, ~13% of the planner's wall time, the stage that was 56% of run cost). Likely cause: painpoints is an array of {text} objects while observations is an array of strings — the asymmetry invites the slip. Change: in the Journal section of .fabro/workflows/develop/prompts/planner.md (and implementer/reviewer), make both plain string arrays (\"painpoints\": [\"<text>\", ...]), or add engine-side repair of trivial syntax errors before spending an output retry. Effect: eliminates a full retry turn per malformed emission. Not a duplicate of fabro-017f (that enforces key presence in the routing validator; this fixes element shape symmetry/repair). Basis: run 01M1RGQHJ5RV8Y28M2GH97XGEZ, workflow version 265a7df1ba6776f527c47bd6508e28afe7b4bdbf83922b13cac16f764b0ff586, commit 309e94fb54c039630f1b6ee81e0d754ec99fdc1e","labels":["revision"]}
